    "updated_at": "2022-05-31T17:18:48Z",
    "body": "So I think using ParseText here is pretty clean, especially since ParseScript seems to really prefer you giving it a Realm (even though it's used just for pass through).\r\n\r\nHowever there may be a slight issue here, which is that ParseText does early-error detection. I wonder if people really plan to do early-error detection (which IIUC involves pretty detailed JavaScript engine semantics) inside the network code where ORB is implemented.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
